From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yewsifofficial <yewsifofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:58:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nex: when no station URL is found, show the bytes instead of
 printing nothing

The last log ran a full match attempt with Register, ReplaceURL and
GetSessionURLs all exchanged, and the station-URL trace printed nothing at
all. Silence has two causes and no way to tell them apart: the patch not
being in that build, or these messages not carrying the URLs as plain
strings where the scan looks for them.

So a message that was expected to hold station URLs and holds none now says
so, with the head of its payload as hex and printable characters. Either the
line is absent, which means the build predates this, or it is there with the
bytes, which says how they are really laid out. One log settles it either
way.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (online play is out of nxnative's scope)
Reason: Nextendo online play for Super Smash Bros. Ultimate
Issue: yewsiff/NX2Apple (no tracker: issues are disabled on this fork)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017xdHQoEipBX2wTqN8BNnMv
---
 dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m b/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
index 4bc5851..b9c2c3d 100644
--- a/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
+++ b/dm/host/net_nextendo_apple.m
@@ -723,7 +723,8 @@ static uint32_t le32(const uint8_t *b) { return (uint32_t)b[0] | (uint32_t)b[1]
 // The station URLs in a message, logged as they stand. They are plain strings in the payload ("address=...;port=...;type=...;Pa=..."), and they
 // are the whole of what a server has to work with when it pairs a private candidate with a public one for a hole punch: which addresses and
 // ports the game registers for itself, and which ones it is given for the other player. Nothing else in these messages is read
-static void nex_stations(const uint8_t *b, unsigned n, const char *what) {
+static int nex_stations(const uint8_t *b, unsigned n, const char *what) {
+    int found = 0;
     for (unsigned i = 0; i + 8 < n; i++) {
         if (memcmp(b + i, "address=", 8)) continue;
         unsigned s0 = i;
@@ -733,8 +734,19 @@ static void nex_stations(const uint8_t *b, unsigned n, const char *what) {
         char t[256]; unsigned len = e - s0 < sizeof t - 1 ? e - s0 : (unsigned)sizeof t - 1;
         memcpy(t, b + s0, len); t[len] = 0;
         LOG("[nextendo] station URL (%s): %s", what, t);
+        found++;
         i = e;
     }
+    // Nothing that looks like one. Either these messages do not carry them in the clear, or they are laid out differently from the assumption
+    // here, and the only way to tell is to see the bytes: the head of the message, printable characters as themselves and the rest as dots
+    if (!found) {
+        char hex[3 * 48 + 1], asc[49];
+        unsigned k = n < 48 ? n : 48;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < k; i++) { snprintf(hex + 3 * i, 4, "%02x ", b[i]); asc[i] = b[i] >= 0x20 && b[i] < 0x7f ? (char)b[i] : '.'; }
+        hex[3 * k] = 0; asc[k] = 0;
+        LOG("[nextendo] no station URL in the %s message (%u bytes); its first %u: %s|%s", what, n, k, hex, asc);
+    }
+    return found;
 }
 // 1 when a line was written. b: the first n bytes of the frame's payload (unmasked), total: the payload's whole length. *split: a split message is passing
 static int nex_note(const uint8_t *b, unsigned n, uint64_t total, int dir, int *split, int quiet) {
